fer Matrix Method for multilayer interference","Quarter-wave transformer principles adapted for broadband minimization"],"expected_advantages":["Potentially better impedance matching at the air interface due to higher initial index step","Different interference phase conditions may align better with the 40-160 nm constraint window than the SiO2-first configuration"],"known_risks":["The high index contrast at the Air/TiO2 interface might dominate losses if the SiO2 layer cannot sufficiently compensate","The optimal thicknesses might fall outside the 40-160 nm bound, limiting performance"],"execution_request_english":"Execute a deterministic TMM optimization for a planar stack with the topology: Incident Medium (Air, n=1.0) | Layer 1 (TiO2, n=2.40, lossless) | Layer 2 (SiO2, n=1.46, lossless) | Substrate (Glass, n=1.52, lossless). Optimize the thicknesses of Layer 1 and Layer 2, constrained between 40 nm and 160 nm inclusive. The objective is to minimize the arithmetic mean power reflectance for s-polarized light at normal incidence (0 degrees) over the wavelength range 450 nm to 700 nm, sampled every 5 nm. Use a deterministic optimizer with seed 17 and a maximum of 64 solver evaluations. Report the full spectrum, optimal thicknesses, and the calculated mean reflectance. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization s. wavelength intervals 450-700 nm. soft objectives: minimize arithmetic mean power reflectance from 450 to 700 nm; achieve mean reflectance below 0.03 as a soft scoring preference. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the 450 to 700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: layer thickness must be between 40 and 160 nm; exactly one layer of SiO2 and one layer of TiO2.","priority":1,"parent_route_id":"route_01","revision_reason":"Per feedback directives and insight appendage, this route swaps the layer order from Round 1 (Air|SiO2|TiO2|Glass) to Air|TiO2|SiO2|Glass to test if the alternative permutation yields a superior global 